  "summary": "The product ships as a CLI and TypeScript SDK; the SDK exposes a CodexSecurity class with run() accepting options like mode, workers, subagents, and maxTimeHours, plus a close() method. A findings service (preview) runs from the same ghcr.io/openai/codex-security image, stores findings and embeddings in SQLite, serves a read-only /dashboard refreshing every five seconds, and returns duplicate candidates by embedding similarity. Evidence coverage: 118 of 143 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
